+            # 0x16 announces a default/registration channel (it reported
+            # ch1=ffff, meaning "none assigned", 48,384 times in 11 hours) and
+            # does not track per-session allocation.
+            #
+            # Layout, confirmed against 8,084 real grants: opcode/flags, mfid,
+            # service options, ch1 (transmit), ch2 (receive, always ffff here),
+            # then the 24-bit target address.
+            # Offsets MATCH op25's own 0x00 grp_v_ch_grant handler, which has
+            # the identical shape (one options octet, channel, channel, 24-bit
+            # address). They were first copied from the 0x16 handler, which has
+            # NO options octet -- everything landed two nibbles out, ch1 decoded
+            # as 0xf9ff (iden 0xf, absent from the freq table), so
+            # channel_id_to_frequency returned None and this whole path went
+            # inert while looking like it was running.
+            mfrid = (tsbk >> 80) & 0xff
+            dso   = (tsbk >> 72) & 0xff
+            ch1   = (tsbk >> 56) & 0xffff
+            ch2   = (tsbk >> 40) & 0xffff
+            llid  = (tsbk >> 16) & 0xffffff
+            freq  = self.channel_id_to_frequency(ch1)
+            if self.debug >= 10:
